d":363,"EventItemActionName":"adopted","EventItemActionText":"This item was adopted.","EventItemPassedFlag":1,"EventItemPassedFlagName":"Pass","EventItemRollCallFlag":0,"EventItemFlagExtra":0,"EventItemTitle":"Settlement of Claim(s) State Farm v. City of Phoenix","EventItemTally":null,"EventItemAccelaRecordId":null,"EventItemConsent":1,"EventItemMoverId":null,"EventItemMover":null,"EventItemSeconderId":null,"EventItemSeconder":null,"EventItemMatterId":35442,"EventItemMatterGuid":"B69E3253-740C-4582-AB53-5039223FC777","EventItemMatterFile":"26-1407","EventItemMatterName":null,"EventItemMatterType":"Payment Ordinance","EventItemMatterStatus":"Adopted","EventItemMatterAttachments":[]},{"EventItemId":64833,"EventItemGuid":"E73EEE0D-DC84-4C6F-9059-D1636BADC514","EventItemLastModifiedUtc":"2026-08-04T16:47:15.863","EventItemRowVersion":"AAAAAASVFl8=","EventItemEventId":2651,"EventItemAgendaSequence":69,"EventItemMinutesSequence":99,"EventItemAgendaNumber":"60","EventItemVideo":null,"EventItemVideoIndex":null,"EventItemVersion":"1","EventItemAgendaNote":null,"EventItemMinutesNote":"{\\rtf1\\ansi\\ansicpg1252\\deff0\\deflang1033{\\fonttbl{\\f0\\fnil\\fcharset0 Arial;}}\r\n{\\colortbl ;\\red0\\green0\\blue0;}\r\n\\viewkind4\\uc1\\pard\\cf1\\b\\fs28 Discussion\\par\r\nMotion was made by Vice Mayor Hodge Washington to approve this item. The motion was seconded by Councilwoman O'Brien.\\b0\\par\r\n\\par\r\nCouncilwoman Hernandez asked how the City measures the impact of arts investments on neighborhood pride, economic activity, and community well-being.\\par\r\n\\par\r\nDeputy City Manager Frank McCune introduced Arts and Culture Interim Director Carrie Brown.\\par\r\n\\par\r\nMs. Brown stated the department uses surveys, focus groups, community conversations during their community presentations, and project assessments. She noted the department really elevated efforts on recent projects based on their grant requirements and implemented those lessons into the public art program. She indicated these efforts are conducted in order to assess community engagement, where input is needed, follow-up planning, as well as to conduct an evaluation of their budget.\\par\r\n\\par\r\nCouncilwoman Hernandez asked whether public art tied to heat mitigation projects are prioritized in high vulnerability neighborhoods which currently have limited shade.\\par\r\n\\par\r\nMs. Brown confirmed these neighborhoods are prioritized and that project locations are selected using heat vulnerability data in coordination with the City\\rquote s heat office. She noted there are other factors they must evaluate as well but the initial locations are based on that data.\\par\r\n\\par\r\nCouncilwoman Hernandez expressed her appreciation for ongoing investments in public art. She highlighted the Rio Reimagined component and noted its importance to her district. She also referenced Item 61, stating that panelists found the recommended applications to be of especially high caliber. She thanked the Arts and Culture Office for its work and voiced her support for the item.\\par\r\n}\r\n","EventItemActionId":363,"EventItemActionName":"adopted","EventItemActionText":"A motion was made by Vice Mayor Hodge Washington, seconded by Councilwoman O'Brien, that this item be adopted. The motion carried by the following vote:","EventItemPassedFlag":1,"EventItemPassedFlagName":"Pass","EventItemRollCallFlag":0,"EventItemFlagExtra":0,"EventItemTitle":"Fiscal Year 2026-31 Public Art Plan (Ordinance S-53082) - Citywide","EventItemTally":null,"EventItemAccelaRecordId":null,"EventItemConsent":0,"EventItemMoverId":2022,"EventItemMover":"Kesha Hodge Washington","EventItemSeconderId":1772,"EventItemSeconder":"Ann O'Brien","EventItemMatterId":35443,"EventItemMatterGuid":"C767B08B-F970-41DB-A20F-140A0EB25A6A","EventItemMatterFile":"26-1408","EventItemMatterName":null,"EventItemMatterType":"Ordinance-S","EventItemMatterStatus":"Adopted","EventItemMatterAttachments":[{"MatterAttachmentId":73848,"Matter